! Sabat II (C-rooted).scl
!
! Marc Sabat, "Well temperament revisited: two tunings for two keyboards
! a quartertone apart in extended JI" (Berlin, 19 February 2019), main
! keyboard of Sabat II.
!
! Sabat notates the tuning normalized from A (1/1 = A, Kammerton A = 0c).
! This build's key table plants degree 0 on the bottom key, which is a C,
! so the published A-rooted list is rotated here by 32/27 (C is 32/27 above
! A) to put each ratio on the key Sabat intended.
!
! Reference pitch is A, which Sabat fixes at the Kammerton (A = 0 cents).
! Tune the A key to 440.000 Hz and every other key falls on the figures
! below; "tuner" is what a chromatic tuner set to A440 will read.
!
! key   degree      ratio to A   Hz (A4=440)   tuner
! C     1/1          32/27          260.741    -5.9
! Db    16/15        512/405        278.123    +5.9
! D     9/8          4/3            293.333    -2.0
! Eb    81/68        24/17          310.588    -3.0
! E     81/64        3/2            330.000    +2.0
! F     4/3          128/81         347.654    -7.8
! F#    729/512      27/16          371.250    +5.9
! G     3/2          16/9           391.111    -3.9
! Ab    51/32        17/9           415.556    +1.0
! A     27/16        1/1            440.000     0.0
! Bb    3645/2048    135/128        464.062    -7.8
! B     243/128      9/8            495.000    +3.9
!
! Other octaves are these figures halved or doubled.  Note that with
! base_units = 485 the bottom C sits at nominal 12-TET, which puts A 5.87
! cents sharp (441.5 Hz); pulling A down to 440 is an absolute-pitch trim on
! the 208p or in the pitch calibration, not a property of this scale.
!
Sabat II (C-rooted)
 12
!
 16/15
 9/8
 81/68
 81/64
 4/3
 729/512
 3/2
 51/32
